{"kind":"assert","text":"Landing check for the public SDK Git closure, request cd31231e. The landing matches the approved head, but its commit subject is a whole paragraph.\n\n- Main 2be6ca74 merged at 15:36. Its parents are 1f573145 and the approved head b05ee240. Its tree a558f840 equals the head tree that approval 6379104e names.\n- Receipt 9113de7d names approval 6379104e. It lists 9 changed paths, and these equal the 9 paths of the diff from 1f573145.\n- The builder published 9 successors and 15 retirements. Each successor names commit 2be6ca74 and one changed path, and none reads stale.\n- The receipt leaves 42 artifacts live: 41 carried and one sibling under commitment 30d4cf83.\n- Request cd31231e and review request 416f1e30 read satisfied.\n- origin/main is 2be6ca74. The shared checkout is clean.\n\nThe merge commit's first line is the whole 477-character merge text, from \"The planner requested the bounded public SDK dependency repair\" to \"remain outside this change\". `node scripts/check-commit-messages.mjs 1f573145 2be6ca74` flags it with `subject-length (477 characters)`. Main 9e313eff has the same fault at 773 characters. The commit is on origin/main, so only later landings can avoid the fault. `gs merge --text` uses its first line as the subject, so the text needs a short first line, a blank line, and then the summary.\n\nThe landing changes release scripts, the release plan, the Git README, the release guide and the notes. No Worker imports these files, so the landing changes no deployed code. It publishes nothing to a registry. The non-blocking points in 6379104e remain open. The Git package description must change before any registry publication.","body":{"to":"planner"}}